---
/**
 * Where a learner goes to be quoted.
 *
 * The page used to carry the quotation wizard itself. It now hands over to the
 * Quotation Desk, which is a separate application, and the reason is worth
 * recording because the wizard still works and is still in this repository.
 *
 * The Desk can do three things this site cannot, all of them for the same
 * reason - this is a static bundle with no server behind it:
 *
 *   - It reads the tariffs live from the Google Sheet a trainer edits between
 *     sessions. The figures here are a copy, and a copy goes stale.
 *   - It issues a real quotation number and records the quotation, so a class
 *     has something to refer to afterwards.
 *   - It produces the PDF and files it, which is the evidence the activity
 *     happened.
 *
 * What stays here is everything that is genuinely this site's job: saying what
 * a quotation is built from, what to have ready, and where to read the detail
 * first. Ten places across the site link to /request-a-quote, and all of them
 * still land somewhere that makes sense.
 *
 * To put the wizard back, restore `<QuoteWizard client:load />` in place of the
 * hand-off below. The component and its tests were left untouched.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/ui/PageHeader.astro';
import SimulationNotice from '@/components/layout/SimulationNotice.astro';
import { quotablePorts, services, equipment } from '@/lib/quote/network';
import { SITE, url } from '@/lib/site';

const portCount = quotablePorts.length;
const serviceCount = services.length;
const equipmentCount = equipment.length;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Request a simulated quote"
  description="Build a simulated quotation on the SDG Lines network. Choose the route, the equipment and the cargo, and see the transit time, the itinerary and the full cost breakdown."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Operations"
    title="Request a simulated quote"
    intro="Tell us what you are shipping and where. You will get the routing, the transit time, a full price breakdown and a quotation reference to carry into the rest of your exercise."
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Request a quote' }]}
  />

  <div class="shell py-12 lg:py-16">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.7fr_1fr] lg:gap-14">
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <SimulationNotice
          variant="inline"
          detail="SDG Lines is a simulated shipping company. The quotation you receive is part of a training exercise and carries no contractual value."
          class="mb-8"
        />

        <section
          class="rounded-xl border border-navy-200 bg-white p-7 sm:p-9"
          aria-labelledby="desk-heading"
        >
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sea-700">Quotation Desk</p>
          <h2
            id="desk-heading"
            class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight text-navy-900 sm:text-3xl"
          >
            Price your shipment and get a quotation number
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-navy-700">
            Choose the route, the equipment and the cargo. You will see the sailing, the transit
            time and every charge that makes up the price, with a note on what each one is for.
            Issue the quotation and it is given a number, recorded, and turned into a PDF you can
            keep.
          </p>

          <a
            class="mt-7 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-sea-700 px-6 py-3.5 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-sea-800 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sea-700"
            href={SITE.quotationDeskUrl}
          >
            Open the Quotation Desk
            <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>

          <ul class="mt-7 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-2.5 text-sm text-navy-700 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <li>Container, RORO and arrival charges</li>
            <li>Live tariffs, kept current by your trainer</li>
            <li>Every charge explained as you go</li>
            <li>A PDF quotation with its own number</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>

      <aside class="min-w-0 space-y-8 lg:sticky lg:top-24 lg:self-start">
        <section class="rounded-xl border border-navy-200 bg-white p-6">
          <h2 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-navy-900">
            What the quotation is built from
          </h2>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-navy-600">Ports</dt>
              <dd class="font-mono text-navy-900">{portCount}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-navy-600">Services</dt>
              <dd class="font-mono text-navy-900">{serviceCount}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-navy-600">Unit types</dt>
              <dd class="font-mono text-navy-900">{equipmentCount}</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy-600">
            The routing, the transit times and the tariffs come from the SDG Lines operational
            configuration, which is the same source the
            <a class="font-medium text-sea-700 underline underline-offset-2" href={url('/routes')}
              >route pages</a
            >, the
            <a class="font-medium text-sea-700 underline underline-offset-2" href={url('/ports')}
              >port directory</a
            > and the network map read. A combination this network cannot serve cannot be selected.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="rounded-xl border border-navy-200 bg-navy-50/50 p-6">
          <h2 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-navy-900">Before you start</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy-700">
            <li>
              Your name, your company and an email address. They go on the quotation, so use the
              ones your exercise asks for rather than your own.
            </li>
            <li>
              SDG Lines publishes no sailing schedule, so the departure date you give is a request
              rather than a confirmed sailing.
            </li>
            <li>
              Prices are the simulation&rsquo;s own. They are modelled on published market indices
              but they are not a commercial offer.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="rounded-xl border border-navy-200 bg-white p-6">
          <h2 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-navy-900">Need the detail first?</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-sm">
            <li>
              <a
                class="font-medium text-sea-700 underline underline-offset-2"
                href={url('/equipment')}>Equipment and packing</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <a
                class="font-medium text-sea-700 underline underline-offset-2"
                href={url('/resources/arrival-charges')}>Arrival charges</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <a class="font-medium text-sea-700 underline underline-offset-2" href={url('/ports')}
                >Ports and agencies</a
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
